-module(libsodium_utils).
-moduledoc """
Constant-time comparisons, little-endian number arithmetic, hexadecimal,
Base64 and IP address codecs, and ISO/IEC 7816-4 padding.

`memcmp/2` and `is_zero/1` run in constant time for a given length and are
the right way to compare secrets such as MACs and keys. `compare/2`,
`increment/1`, `add/2`, and `sub/2` treat their binaries as unsigned
little-endian numbers (the layout of libsodium nonces and counters) and also
run in constant time for a given length. Functions taking two binaries
raise `badarg` unless both have the same length.

Base64 functions take a variant from `base64_variants/0` (or its libsodium
integer value) and default to `original`. Decoding functions return `-1`
for malformed input.

```erlang
Hex = libsodium_utils:bin2hex(<<"hi">>),
<<"6869">> = Hex,
<<"hi">> = libsodium_utils:hex2bin(Hex),
<<"aGk">> = libsodium_utils:bin2base64(<<"hi">>, urlsafe_no_padding),
<<"hi">> = libsodium_utils:base642bin(<<"aGk">>, urlsafe_no_padding),
<<1, 1>> = libsodium_utils:increment(<<0, 1>>),
0 = libsodium_utils:memcmp(<<"secret">>, <<"secret">>).
```
""".
-moduledoc #{author => ["Andrew Bennett <potatosaladx@gmail.com>"]}.
